 "text": "Honey Nut Cheerios has more sugar than honey. Sugar is the second ingredient. Honey is further down and there's brown sugar syrup after that. General Mills says the 12 grams of sugar in a serving come from sugar, real honey, and brown sugar syrup and it's 24% of your recommended daily amount. There are no nuts in it either. The nut in honey nut is natural almond flavour, which is why the allergen line says contains almond ingredients instead of contains almonds. The box says made with real honey. That's true, it just isn't the main sweetener.",
